      "nets": ["/NET0025", "/NET0032", "/NET0028", "/NET0037", "/NET0021", "/NET0010"],
      "observed": "The zero-ohm resistors R23 and R6 connect M5 bus pins 19 and 21 together, with the joined node feeding the PWM signal through R17. Likewise, R14 and R8 connect pins 20 and 22 together, with the joined node feeding the other PWM signal through R20.",
      "expected": "Only one bus pin from each alternative pair should be connected to its PWM channel. The specification says the 0-ohm jumpers select between pins 19/21 for channel 1 and pins 20/22 for channel 2, with a different pair used for different M5Stack variants.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/NET0025\") ... (node (ref \"J10\") (pin \"19\")) ... (node (ref \"R23\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/NET0028\") ... (node (ref \"J10\") (pin \"21\")) ... (node (ref \"R6\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/NET0032\") ... (node (ref \"R23\") (pin \"1\")) ... (node (ref \"R6\") (pin \"1\")) ... (node (ref \"R17\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/NET0037\") ... (node (ref \"J10\") (pin \"20\")) ... (node (ref \"R14\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/NET0010\") ... (node (ref \"J10\") (pin \"22\")) ... (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (name \"/NET0021\") ... (node (ref \"R14\") (pin \"1\")) ... (node (ref \"R8\") (pin \"1\")) ... (node (ref \"R20\") (pin \"2\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R9–R12 | 0 Ω (jumpers) | Select which M5Stack bus pin (pin 19/21 for ch.1, pin 20/22 for ch.2) supplies PWM1/PWM2"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Short R10, R10 for Core2 and CoreS3 / Short R9, R11 for others"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Each PWM channel ties together two distinct M5Stack GPIO bus pins rather than selecting one. This can cause GPIO output contention or unintended loading, and can prevent reliable PWM control or interfere with other functions using those pins.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows both alternatives in each PWM GPIO selection pair connected through zero-ohm resistors. This contradicts the specified mutually exclusive jumper selection and risks shorting distinct GPIO outputs together."
}

